This happense because n is a decimal number, this result can be generalized to any base representationfor example 101 is 5 in base 2 Adding 1 after performing greatest integer function, we get numb digits = 3. Which is true for binary we only have 3 digits.This method is unreliable and only works for This only works for such numbers because logarithm is not defined for numbers less than equal to zero. This is also not applicable on non integers. This can produce wrong results due to floating point precisions. But the method works fine for the int range.

